*---------------------- METADATA FIELD

#TITLE 48 KEY Keyboard Test (DP)
#SUBTITLE 48 KEY DP — channels 11..19 + 1A..1O and 21..29 + 2A..2O
#ARTIST be-music
#GENRE TEST
#BPM 120
#PLAYLEVEL 5
#TOTAL 400
#DIFFICULTY 3

*---------------------- EXTENDED HEADER FIELD
* Keyboardmania-style 48 KEY DP — the 24 KEY SP bank mirrored onto the
* 2P side (`21..29` + `2A..2O`). Un-hand-playable by design; it exists so
* AUTO PLAY and the renderer can be checked against the widest lane set
* the engine supports.
*
* `#PLAYER 3` is the usual DP marker, and it also feeds the POPN-9 rule
* "`#PLAYER 3` + channel `17` → 9 KEY". Extended lane channels are
* checked FIRST, so this chart resolves to `'48'` rather than `'9'` —
* that precedence is the regression this fixture guards.
*
* This chart exists to validate:
*   - `48 KEY DP` lane-mode detection across both sides
*   - extended-lane precedence over the `#PLAYER 3` + `17` POPN-9 rule
*   - per-side lane ordering / side split on the fallback playfield

#PLAYER 3
#LNTYPE 1
#LNMODE 1
#LNOBJ ZZ

*---------------------- RESOURCES FIELD

#WAV01 sample.wav
#WAVZZ sample.wav

